# Typography bible (Taxi-driver-page)

Apply these principles whenever you add or change layout, copy, styles, or components.

## 1. Readable fonts

- **One text family:** Open Sans (`font-sans`, `var(--font-family-sans)`) with Arial/Helvetica fallback — already in `src/styles/typography.css`.
- **Icons only:** Font Awesome 6 Brands (`.fa-brand`, `.icon-brand-*`) for social/brand glyphs — not for body text.
- Do not introduce extra display or script fonts without explicit user approval.

## 2. Don’t overboard on fonts

- Max **one sans stack + icon font**. No mixing third-party text faces.
- Use **weight 400** by default; heavier weights only for clear hierarchy (one step up, e.g. semibold on a single H1).

## 3. Clear hierarchy

- **One primary H1** per page; logical heading order (h1 → h2 → h3).
- Map roles to tokens: headings `text-fg-gray-900` / `text-fg-black`, body `text-fg-ink`, secondary `text-fg-gray-500` / `text-fg-secondary`, accents `text-fg-amber` / `text-fg-green` sparingly.
- Size steps: responsive body (`var(--font-size-base)` in `responsive-type.css`) + fixed presets (`.type-14`, `.type-12-8`, `.type-11-2`) for UI chrome — don’t invent random `text-[13px]` unless matching spec.

## 4. Breathing room

- Prefer generous **padding/margin** on sections (`gap`, `py`, `px`) over tight walls of text.
- Pair line-height utilities (`.lh-22`–`.lh-28`) with dense blocks; body uses **1.15** ratio — don’t crush multi-line paragraphs.

## 5. Letter spacing

- Default tracking for body; use **`tracking-wide` / uppercase** only for short labels (e.g. one-line kicker), not paragraphs.
- If uppercase, keep copy **short** and increase tracking slightly — never uppercase long sentences.

## 6. Alignment

- **Left-align** body copy (LTR). Center only headlines/CTAs when design calls for it — keep blocks consistent within a section.
- Use flex/grid alignment so icons + text baselines line up (e.g. `items-center` on icon rows).

## 7. Contrast

- Use **`text-fg-*` on appropriate backgrounds** — e.g. `text-fg-white` / `text-fg-pale` only on dark bands (`bg-fg-gray-900`, `bg-black`).
- Avoid `text-fg-muted` on `bg-surface-muted` for essential content; reserve low-contrast pairs for non-critical meta.
- Aim for WCAG-friendly pairs on CTAs (amber/yellow buttons: dark text on `brand-yellow`, not pale gray on yellow).

## 8. All devices

- **Mobile-first:** body scales 14px → 22px via `src/styles/responsive-type.css` — don’t override `body` font-size in components without reason.
- Test layouts at **&lt;640, 768, 1024, 1280, 1536**; fixed `.type-*` and icon sizes stay px — ensure they still fit on small screens (wrap, don’t overflow).

## 9. ALL CAPS sparingly

- No shouting: caps for **tiny labels only** (≤ few words), not headings or body.
- Prefer sentence case for headings and buttons unless brand requires otherwise.

## 10. Before shipping UI

- Hierarchy obvious at a glance? Contrast OK on mobile? One font family? Spacing consistent? Then ship.

**Source of truth:** `src/styles/global.css` (colors), `typography.css` (type + icons), `responsive-type.css` (breakpoints).
